# Module and Submodule Shell Consolidation

## Context
Conventional child routes can override outer width, padding, or global layout mode, causing their back links and content to drift from the Store Orders reference layout.

## Goal
- Give conventional module-depth routes one stable outer navigation rail and one inset content rail.
- Keep route chrome ownership centralized and make module adapters reusable across child routes.
- Record route-family shell ownership so specialized canvases, documents, and side-navigation pages remain intentional.

## Non-Goals
- Redesign immersive editors, document readers, or page-builder canvases.
- Change backend domain behavior.

## Steps
1. Inventory registered routes and classify their shell owner.
2. Consolidate Store child routes on `ModulePageShell` through `StorePageShell`.
3. Remove routed-component layout-mode mutations and centralize pathname policy.
4. Align side-navigation shell rails and document the route-family contract.
5. Add focused tests and run frontend policy, test, lint, and build checks.

## Verification
- Focused shell and route-policy tests.
- Frontend test suite, lint, build, and policy checks.
- Correctness scan for remaining routed-component layout-mode mutations and shell geometry overrides.

